#### 10. Inappropriate use of FRV information technology systems
**10.1 Scope** – FRV IT systems are business tools; limited personal use is permitted if it doesn't affect work performance or breach policy. Includes computers/servers/PCs, email and messaging, internet, screen savers, wallpaper, bulletin boards, file storage, communication systems and fax machines.

**10.2 Policy** – FRV systems must not be used for any inappropriate purpose or Unacceptable Behaviour (storing, saving, displaying, downloading, printing, receiving or sending). This includes material that:
- intimidates, insults, offends or humiliates on the basis of sexual orientation, gender, race, age, physical features, national or ethnic origin, religious or political beliefs, disability or any other protected attribute;
- is obscene or sexually offensive (including sexual jokes and cartoons, even if not pornographic);
- is defamatory;
- is abusive, offensive, insulting, threatening or invades privacy;
- disrupts the workplace (excessive personal use, mass mailing of jokes, chain letters) or could be a criminal offence;
- infringes intellectual property/copyright;
- is unsolicited ("spamming" or "letter bombing");
- represents a personal opinion as FRV's opinion;
- misuses the system (tampering, viruses, unauthorised access to another person's email, documents or computer use);
- accesses inappropriate sites – adult entertainment, sexual violence, pornography, illicit drugs, illegal activities, militancy/terrorism, racism, violence, weaponry and gambling.

**10.3 Access and monitoring** – FRV may at any time, **without first giving notice**: monitor, access and copy emails, internet and computer usage; filter and block offensive emails, attachments or sites; censor and screen offensive or non-business material; provide access and copies to law enforcement if illegal or criminal acts are suspected. Complying with this is a condition of using FRV systems.

**10.4 Confidentiality and complaints** – contents remain confidential except for disciplinary investigations, legal proceedings or law enforcement. Breaches may lead to disciplinary action including termination. Messages from employee representatives are permitted only where authorised by the relevant **Union Secretary**. Complaints are dealt with through the Issue Resolution Procedure.
